  "title": "Why Use Functions? — DRY & Modularity",
  "subtitle": "Clean Software Architecture Principles",
  "topic": "6.2 • DRY PRINCIPLE & ARCHITECTURE",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      6.2 • Best Practices\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>DRY</hlt> Principle\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      <strong>DRY</strong> stands for <em>\"Don't Repeat Yourself\"</em>. If you write the same calculation 5 times, a bug fix requires editing 5 places. Functions create a single source of truth!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #c4b5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Engineering Benefits\n    </span>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 12px; font-size: 13px;\">\n        <strong>1. Maintainability:</strong> Change logic in one function definition, and all 100 call sites update instantly.\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 12px; font-size: 13px;\">\n        <strong>2. Readability:</strong> <code>validate_payment()</code> tells readers what happens without exposing 50 lines of math.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}